speechtext:
The purpose of the vote is for the inspection and treatment, if required, of imports and exports of plants and plant products for insect pests and plant diseases; in cooperation with the British Ministry of Food, inspection of ships at maritime ports for insect infestation,	and	the supervision
and treatment when required prior to loading of food	and plant products;
in cooperation with the division of entomology the inspection of grain elevators, warehouses, dehydration plants and grain storage ships in great lakes ports for insect pests, and supervision and treatment when necessary; to maintain essential seed supplies inspection in the field, in storage and at shipping points of potatoes entered for certification as seed potatoes, in cooperation with the Department of Trade and Commerce and with the marketing service of the Department of Agriculture; the promotion of the export trade in seed potatoes; potato tuber indexing in greenhouses during winter, to assist growers in the prevention of disease from potato stock; issuance of certificates of health for plants and plant products to meet requirements of importing countries; maintenance of quarantines under the Destructive Insects and Pests Act; the eradication or control of foreign insect and plant diseases, established in Canada, including the Japanese beetle.
